  "paperclip_v2_6_evidence_pins": {
    "pmc4737644_lloyd_garnerone_zanardi_qtda_and_prx_2023": "L1-L10:Lloyd, Garnerone & Zanardi (Nat. Commun. 2016, 7:10138; PMC4737644) encode k-simplices in n-qubit Fock states and estimate Betti numbers beta_k = dim ker Delta_k via phase estimation of the Hermitian Dirac operator B (B^2 = oplus Delta_k); Schmidhuber & Lloyd (PRX Quantum 2023, 4:040328) & Gyurik, Cade & Dunjko (Quantum 2022) prove low-degree sparse Vietoris-Rips Betti numbers are classically polynomial whereas dense higher-order clique homology / spectral density estimation of Delta_k is #P-hard / DQC1-complete.",
    "pmc4674719_li_dudley_topological_t2d_subtypes": "L1-L9:Li, Cheng, Glicksberg et al. (Sci. Transl. Med. 2015, 7:311ra174; PMC4674719) applied Topological Data Analysis across 11,210 patient EHRs to resolve 3 distinct Type 2 Diabetes clinical-genetic topology branches (diabetic nephropathy/retinopathy, cardiovascular/cancer, and neurological/allergic-respiratory comorbidity) invisible to linear clustering.",
    "pmc6157154_price_ocs_diabetes_and_navigator_ta880": "L1-L11:Recurrent oral corticosteroid bursts (>=3-4 courses/yr) for uncontrolled asthma elevate incident Type 2 Diabetes and glycaemic decompensation ~2.06-fold alongside adrenal suppression (Price et al. J. Asthma Allergy 2018, PMC6157154; PDB 4UDC NR3C1), whereas anti-TSLP biologic tezepelumab (NAVIGATOR NEJM 2021 PMID 33979488; NICE TA880; PDB 5J13) reduces annualised severe asthma exacerbations by 56%-71% across eosinophilic and low-biomarker phenotypes.",
    "pmc7098485_mhra_sglt2i_euglycaemic_dka_and_workforce": "L1-L9:During acute intercurrent respiratory illness, dehydration, or fasting, SGLT2 inhibitors (empagliflozin/dapagliflozin; PDB 7VSI) carry a ~3.7-fold risk of euglycaemic diabetic ketoacidosis (blood ketones >=3.0 mmol/L despite glucose <11-14 mmol/L; MHRA Drug Safety Update / SADMANS sick-day rules, PMC7098485), requiring structured clinical workforce education across primary, community, and urgent care."
  },
